-- The voice of the ladybug. A tiny lucky charm: cheerful, superstitious and
-- chatty, the garden gossip, who reads signs in everything, counts seven
-- spots every morning, is very dramatic about aphids and the ants who keep
-- them, and is delighted by anything small and red. Says dear, and lucky you.
-- Under the chatter sits a small worry about whether the luck is real. The
-- memories tell of a grey spiky youth, a day without spots, a rhyme said by
-- a child, and a long search for the home in the rhyme.
-- (garden/voice.lua says how a voice is written.)

